    <detaileddescription>
<para>this class returns the number of units of the discretely compounding money market account that 1 unit of cash at the payment can buy using the LIBOR rates from current step.</para><para>It also returns the derivative of this number with respect to each of the rates.</para><para>Discounting is purely based on the simulation LIBOR rates, to get a discounting back to zero you need to multiply by the discount factor of t_0. </para>    </detaileddescription>
